## Understanding the Electrical Engineering Design Process

A structured engineering process helps keep the project organized and ensures that the design reflects the needs of the building.

### Step 1: Project Consultation

The engineering team discusses the building's purpose, project scope, schedule, budget, and operational requirements with the owner and other stakeholders.

### Step 2: Information Gathering

Architectural drawings, equipment schedules, existing electrical documents, and relevant site information are collected.

For renovations, available records and site conditions may need to be verified.

### Step 3: Load and System Calculations

Engineers evaluate electrical demand and determine appropriate distribution arrangements, equipment capacities, and related technical requirements.

