### Step 4: Preliminary Design

Initial layouts establish the locations of major electrical equipment, distribution routes, lighting fixtures, and other system components.

The preliminary design is coordinated with architectural and MEP plans.

### Step 5: Detailed Design Development

The engineering team develops drawings, calculations, schedules, and specifications suitable for the agreed project scope.

Applicable codes and project requirements are incorporated into the design.

### Step 6: Coordination and Quality Review

The documents are reviewed for consistency, technical quality, and potential conflicts with other building systems.

Design adjustments may be made in response to project-team feedback.

### Step 7: Construction Documentation

The completed documents communicate the intended electrical design to the contractor and other relevant participants.

The level of detail depends on the contract, project type, and applicable submission requirements.

### Step 8: Construction-Phase Coordination

Where included in the agreement, the engineering team may review relevant submittals, answer technical questions, and evaluate proposed changes.

The purpose is to help ensure that construction remains consistent with the design intent and approved project requirements.

